course: dictionary
lesson: 13439
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word horseshoes can mean metal plates for a horse's hooves, or a game played outdoors. To know which meaning is right, read the words around it. «The blacksmith nailed new horseshoes onto the farm horse's hooves.» Blacksmith, horse and hooves are the clues, so horseshoes must be the metal plates.
explain: «Mia and Sam played horseshoes in the garden all afternoon.» Played is the clue here. You play a game, not a horse, so horseshoes means the game. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Words can also carry a shape or a feeling. A horseshoe is shaped like a U, and people often hang one over a door because it is a sign of good luck. When you find a word with more than one meaning, pick the one that fits the clues best, and check a dictionary if you are not sure.
fact: A horseshoe is a U-shaped metal plate nailed to the bottom of a horse's hooves to protect them.
fact: In the USA and Canada, horseshoes is also the name of a game where players throw horseshoes at a metal stake in the ground.
fact: Horseshoes can also mean something shaped like a U, such as a horseshoe magnet.
fact: A horseshoe is a sign of good luck, which is why people hang one over a door.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is a word with more than one sense. Context tells you which sense is meant.
exercise: «The blacksmith nailed new horseshoes onto the farm horse's hooves.» What are horseshoes in this sentence? | *U-shaped metal plates for a horse's hooves | Soft shoes for riding | Wooden fences around the field | Sweets for horses
exercise: «Mia and Sam played horseshoes in the garden all afternoon.» Which meaning fits best? | A kind of hat worn in the sun | A type of lunch | A long walk around the farm | *A game where players throw horseshoes at a metal stake
exercise: Dad hung a horseshoe over the door for good luck. What shape is a horseshoe? | Straight like a stick | Round like a ball | *U-shaped | Square like a box
test: «A horse has four hooves, so it needs four horseshoes.» How many horseshoes does a horse need? | Two | Eight | *Four | Six
test: Ella says horseshoes are the same as shoes for people. What is wrong with that? | Nothing is wrong with it | They are worn on the head | They are soft slippers for walking indoors | *They are metal plates for horses' hooves, not shoes you wear
exam: Jayden says, «Horseshoes are the best part of summer camp.» Which meaning is most likely? | A U-shaped magnet in a science lab | A lucky charm for a pet dog | *A game played outdoors at summer camp | Metal plates on a horse's hooves in a stable
